      "writtenOn": "2024-11-22T19:24:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would a `boolean` method be sufficient for your use case? E.g., `boolean verifySigningInfoMatchExactly(path1, path2)`?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11889,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 11889,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "137d9e60f363e71a14ae732d8312153a642053ba",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e050a70_f81ee66a",
        "filename": "core/java/android/content/pm/PackageManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 11889,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-22T19:54:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason why we need to expose this as an API rather than having Package Manager verify the signature is more flexibility (see go/art-cloud-compilation-platform-design#heading\u003dh.ewbre2rq8kcr). A boolean won\u0027t give us this flexibility.",
      "parentUuid": "e329f05e_6216c279",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11889,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 11889,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "137d9e60f363e71a14ae732d8312153a642053ba",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3fd03107_26685dbf",
        "filename": "core/java/android/content/pm/PackageManager.java",
