      "lineNbr": 11889,
      "author": {
        "id": 1047684
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-25T11:37:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As discussed last Thursday, the verb should be `get` instead of `verify`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11889,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 11889,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "137d9e60f363e71a14ae732d8312153a642053ba",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c20305df_d3e221dc",
        "filename": "core/java/android/content/pm/PackageManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 11889,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-25T12:00:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We haven\u0027t discussed this thoroughly. I think it\u0027s important to use `verify` because:\n\n1. The operation involves a signature verification, not just blindly returning any signature. In order words, this method only returns the signature if the verification passes.\n2. The word `get` may sound like the method is just a getter, while the method is actually quite expensive because it needs to verify the signature.",
      "parentUuid": "3fd03107_26685dbf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11889,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 11889,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "137d9e60f363e71a14ae732d8312153a642053ba",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e23022e_06c74fb4",
        "filename": "core/java/android/content/pm/PackageManager.java",
